.TH CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_RESUME 3 "2026-07-18" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_event_loop_resume \- resume event delivery for a registration previously paused by ccol_event_loop_pause
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_event_loop_resume(ccol_event_loop loop, ccol_event_reg reg);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
fd-only: called on a registration built from a queue/ccol_channel selectable,
returns ccol_invalid_args, same restriction as ccol_event_loop_modify.

Recomputes the fd's combined epoll interest mask to include reg
again: an ordinary EPOLL_CTL_MOD call if the fd is still present in the
kernel's own epoll interest set (the other direction on the same fd,
if any, was already live and unpaused), or an EPOLL_CTL_ADD if
ccol_event_loop_pause had removed the fd from that set entirely (every
direction was paused).  reg's direction, generation, and
ccol_event_loop_reg_count contribution are all unchanged from before the
pause; this call only reverses what ccol_event_loop_pause did to the
interest mask.

Resuming a reg that is not currently paused (never paused, or already
resumed) is a no-op success.  This deliberately mirrors
ccol_event_loop_modify's own "already in the requested state" idempotence
rather than treating it as an error.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop  ccol_event_loop the registration belongs to.
reg   Registration to resume.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        Resumed (or was not paused to begin with).
ccol_invalid_args   loop is CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_INVALID or a stale/already-
                    destroyed handle; reg is CCOL_EVENT_REG_INVALID or
                    otherwise fails to resolve; or reg is a queue/
                    ccol_channel registration.  reg failing to resolve
                    covers the case where it was concurrently removed
                    (e.g. the connection was closed while the caller
                    still thought it owned a paused registration to
                    resume).
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call concurrently with ccol_event_loop_remove() and from within a
callback running on one of the reactor threads.  Commonly called from
a different thread than the one that paused reg; see
ccol_event_loop_pause(3)'s own EXAMPLES.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_event_loop_pause (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_add (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_remove (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_modify (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_reg_generation (3)
